  m_Name: 1200 orang laut
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: Respect for Elders - 19th Century
  info: 'Rooted in Confucian values brought by Chinese immigrants, respect for elders
    became a fundamental social norm. Children are expected to show deference through
    gestures like addressing elders with honorifics and offering seats to them in
    public spaces. This tradition continues to shape intergenerational relationships
    in Singaporean society.  '
